    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p>You can clean the print head nozzles using the control panel on your product.</p>
      </context>
      <steps id="steps_05013272">
         <step>
            <cmd>Make sure there are no errors on the LCD screen and the output tray is extended.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Load a few sheets of plain paper in the product.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Press the <image height="13" href="../media/image65.png" placement="break" width="17">
                  <alt>placeholder</alt>
               </image> home button, if necessary.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select <b>Maintenance</b>&gt; <b>Head</b>
               <b>Cleaning</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>placeholder</title>
                  <image height="199" href="../media/image184.jpeg" placement="break" width="199">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Press the <image height="11" href="../media/image47.png" placement="break" width="11">
                  <alt>placeholder</alt>
               </image> start button to clean the print head. You see a message on the LCD screen during the cleaning cycle.</cmd>
            <info>
               <p>The <image height="12" href="../media/image185.png" placement="break" width="12">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image> power light flashes throughout the cleaning cycle and stays on when the cleaning cycle is finished. When the cleaning cycle is finished, you see a message on the screen and a nozzle pattern prints.</p>
               <note type="caution">Never turn off the product or open the scanner unit during a cleaning cycle or you may not be able to print.</note>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Check the printed pattern to see if there are gaps in the lines.</cmd>
